{"custom_id": "370d35743db291ba4f5875c7ca8ae3a0dffd7a7e88eee95b", "meta": {"loop": "S-r02-S-10767339", "task": "annotate_with_guidelines", "occurrence": 0, "attempt": 0, "max_tokens": 128000, "prompt_sha256": "6133e0bdd944f9ceace74db6769a9756af10d49564a3476337ec7e3b3ec8e519", "prompt_chars": 10198}, "batch_id": "msgbatch_01CExDSRTBhn68TSGCQpcsij", "saved_utc": "2026-11-13T22:23:02+00:00", "message": {"id": "msg_011Ch1eb4HX3F3uLDiJ4SWj2", "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "I'm scanning the title and abstract for disease mentions, starting with \"FMR1 deficiency\" in the title as a candidate specific disease, then \"fragile X syndrome\" and \"mental retardation\" in the abstract.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"annotations\":[{\"start\":20,\"end\":35,\"text\":\"FMR1 deficiency\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"FMR1 deficiency names one specific disease state (loss of FMR1 function, i.e. fragile X), analogous to C7 deficiency in the guidelines. The bare word deficiency is excluded, but the compound refers to a single specific disease.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 - Specific Disease; Examples 6\"},{\"start\":92,\"end\":110,\"text\":\"Fragile X syndrome\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Fragile X syndrome is a single, well-defined genetic disease with no further categorization, so it is a Specific Disease mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 - Specific Disease\"},{\"start\":132,\"end\":150,\"text\":\"mental retardation\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Mental retardation refers to a broad family of intellectual disability conditions with many possible causes, a grey-area term treated as a Disease Class, as in the guidelines' X-linked mental retardation example.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 - Disease Class; Examples 11-12\"},{\"start\":377,\"end\":391,\"text\":\"macroorchidism\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Macroorchidism (abnormally enlarged testes) is a specific, clinically defined condition with a single definition, described here as a feature of the fragile X phenotype.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 - Specific Disease\"},{\"start\":543,\"end\":561,\"text\":\"fragile X syndrome\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Fragile X syndrome is a single, well-defined genetic disease with no further categorization, so it is a Specific Disease mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 - Specific Disease\"},{\"start\":1046,\"end\":1061,\"text\":\"Macro-orchidism\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Macro-orchidism is a specific, clinically defined condition with a single definition, described here as a phenotype of knockout mice carrying the YAC transgene.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 - Specific Disease\"},{\"start\":1210,\"end\":1219,\"text\":\"fragile X\",\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"Fragile X is a disease name used as a modifier of the noun patients (fragile X patients), so it is annotated as a Modifier.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 3 - Modifiers\"},{\"start\":1780,\"end\":1798,\"text\":\"fragile X syndrome\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Fragile X syndrome is a single, well-defined genetic disease with no further categorization, so it is a Specific Disease mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 - Specific Disease\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4186, "output_tokens": 11146, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 10171}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}